XnuPrelink 440589b (+ fixture, local-relocation and vtable patches): kernel HMAC on macOS collections, root CPU subtype

1. Kernel corecrypto HMAC: resealing is skipped only when neither the native
   kernel nor the replaced com.apple.kernel entry carries __fips_hmacs (macOS
   27.3 seals corecrypto in com.apple.kec.corecrypto, handled by
   seal_components). This change was used from run 23 on but was missing from
   arm64-local-relocations.patch; it is published here.

2. Root header CPU subtype:

DarwinBoot's ParseKernel requires the MH_FILESET root header and its
com.apple.kernel entry to carry the same cpusubtype. The NABU kernel is plain
arm64 (0x0) while the original macOS 27.3 collection header says arm64e
(0xc0000002), so DarwinBoot would refuse every nabu candidate. The emitter now
writes the native kernel's subtype into the root header (the collection runs
that kernel); every original kext entry keeps its own arm64e subtype. A CPU
type mismatch still stops emission.

Checked with lab/nabu/darwinboot_check.py (offline replica of DarwinBoot
3c75734): before, rejected (subtype mismatch); after, accepted.
---
diff --git a/fileset_segmented.py b/fileset_segmented.py
index 1bdee73..35f5218 100644
--- a/fileset_segmented.py
+++ b/fileset_segmented.py
@@ -298,6 +298,16 @@ class SegmentedEmit(Emit):
         # corecrypto authenticates the relocated __text bytes in a fileset.
         code = next(s for s in self.native.sections if s['segment'] == '__TEXT_EXEC' and s['name'] == '__text')
         seals = [s for s in self.native.sections if s['name'] == '__fips_hmacs']
+        if not seals:
+            # macOS collections seal corecrypto in com.apple.kec.corecrypto
+            # (seal_components), not in the kernel. Skip only when the replaced
+            # kernel entry carried no seal either.
+            old_kernel = Image(self.cache.data, self.cache.entries['com.apple.kernel'][1])
+            if any(s['name'] == '__fips_hmacs' for s in old_kernel.sections):
+                raise ValueError('Original kernel carries a corecrypto HMAC field; the native kernel has none')
+            self.report['corecrypto_hmac_sha256'] = None
+            self.report['corecrypto_hmac_location'] = 'not in kernel (original and native kernels carry no __fips_hmacs)'
+            return
         if len(seals) != 1 or seals[0]['size'] != 32:
             raise ValueError('Expected one 32-byte corecrypto HMAC field')
         code_at = self.layout.translate(code['va']) - self.cache.base
@@ -384,5 +394,18 @@ class SegmentedEmit(Emit):
             raise ValueError('Root commands exceed header mapping')
         self.data[32:limit] = payload + bytes(limit-32-len(payload))
         struct.pack_into('<II', self.data, 16, len(rebuilt), len(payload))
+        # The collection runs the native kernel: its root header carries the
+        # kernel's CPU subtype. A plain arm64 kernel (subtype 0) in an arm64e
+        # collection keeps every original entry at its own arm64e subtype;
+        # DarwinBoot requires the root and com.apple.kernel subtypes to agree.
+        cpu, subtype = struct.unpack_from('<Ii', self.native.data, 4)
+        root_cpu, root_subtype = struct.unpack_from('<Ii', self.data, 4)
+        if cpu != root_cpu:
+            raise ValueError('Native kernel and collection CPU types differ')
+        if subtype != root_subtype:
+            struct.pack_into('<i', self.data, 8, subtype)
+            self.report['root_cpusubtype'] = {'original': hex(root_subtype & 0xffffffff),
+                                              'written': hex(subtype & 0xffffffff),
+                                              'reason': 'matches the native com.apple.kernel entry'}
         self.report['native_base'] = hex(self.layout.placements['__TEXT'])
         self.report['native_fileoff'] = hex(self.fileoff)
